@startuml
title Choosing a NativeEval Form — Four Mutually Exclusive Alternatives
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FDE68A
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #B45309
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #F1F5F9
skinparam NoteBorderColor #94A3B8

start

:An extender fragment declares
""semantics <LanguageExpr>""
//optional; defaults to// ""Rust"";<<#FDE68A>>
note right
  The ""semantics"" clause names the language the block
  is written in and scopes the reading of every ""![ … ]""
  beneath it. ""Rust"" is the //bootstrap// default because
  Rust is the only semantics that exists today (§V.1).
end note

:A rule, literal, or token carries a native block
""Add . a:Int, b:Int |- a &#34;+&#34; b : Int  ![a + b] fold"";<<#FEE2E2>>

if (Is the body a single application of one operator\nfrom the closed alphabet to its declared operands?) then (**yes** — 69 of 245 bodies)
  :**""(&#34;op&#34;, name)""**
  closed algebra: add sub mul div mod neg
  eq ne lt gt le ge · and or xor not · concat len
  **needs no semantics target at all**;<<#DCFCE7>>
  :""rho_binop"" / ""rho_unop"" derive the meaning
  from the //syntax terminal//, never from the body
  <latex>\rightarrow \texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex> scalar contract;<<#BFDBFE>>
  note right
    §I.5 is why this form needs no semantics target: the
    rho-native lowering //already// ignores the host body and
    reads the operator terminal out of the syntax pattern.
    ""(&#34;op&#34;, …)"" merely //states// what the lowering infers.
  end note
elseif (Is it a ""literals{}"" eval body — a named framework\nparser applied to the matched text?) then (**yes** — 13 of 13)
  :**""(&#34;carrier&#34;, kind, params)""**
  ""(&#34;carrier&#34;, &#34;int&#34;, {&#34;suffix&#34;: &#34;i32&#34;})""
  **needs no semantics target at all**;<<#DCFCE7>>
  :""NativeKind"" + the fixed set of framework
  literal parsers (""parse_int_lit"", ""parse_rational_lit"",
  ""parse_fixed_lit"", …);<<#BFDBFE>>
elseif (Does the node already register an evaluator\nof the right arity under a fingerprint-scoped URN?) then (**yes** — the long tail, by name)
  :**""(&#34;handler&#34;, urn)""**
  ""mtl:native:{fingerprint}:{Category}_{Label}""
  a //name//, never a body;<<#DDD6FE>>
  :""NativeHandlerSpec""
  <latex>\texttt{Arc<dyn Fn(\&[GroundTerm]) \rightarrow Option<GroundTerm>>}</latex>
  dispatch channel and ""body_ref"" **fingerprint-scoped**
  ★ //required; at the verification base they are NOT —//
  //""native_contract_channel"" keys on the bare rule index//;<<#BFDBFE>>
  note right
    An **unregistered** URN makes the rule //inert//: the evaluator
    yields ""None"" and the redex is left unreduced. That is the
    same fold-gate semantics as an arithmetic overflow or a
    non-value operand — a specification cannot conjure behaviour
    by naming a handler. ★ What this form does //not// give you:
    the URN commits to a **language identity**, not to the
    evaluator's own code, so **G4 must also bind a THIRD-PARTY
    content-hash commitment** — registry-published, or carried
    by the URN band. A commitment supplied by the specification
    would let the attacker supply both sides of the equality.
  end note
else (**otherwise** — the bootstrap escape)
  :**""(&#34;src&#34;, semantics, text)""**
  source text in the named semantics language
  ""(&#34;src&#34;, &#34;Rust&#34;, &#34;mettail_runtime::numeric_int_bin_i32(a, w)&#34;)"";<<#FCA5A5>>
  :""semantics = Rust"": project to ""language!"" and
  compile — **a Rust toolchain is required at install time**
  ""semantics"" <latex>\neq</latex> ""Rust"": **fail-closed**
  **and it is never registry-publishable**: G4 rejects it
  whenever the CALL SITE passed ""Provenance::NonLocal"";<<#FCA5A5>>
endif

:The rule now has a declarative evaluation form.
A specification whose //every// NativeEval avoids ""(&#34;src&#34;, …)""
is **installation-pure**: elaborable and installable
with no compiler in the loop.
**25 of the 31 shipped languages qualify (81%)**;<<#A7F3D0>>

stop

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept (pinned palette, diagrams/PALETTE.md) |
  |<#FDE68A> | **P1** L0 authoring surface — the ""semantics"" clause |
  |<#FEE2E2> | **P6** Host-embedding source, as written today |
  |<#DCFCE7> | **P5** Fully declarative — needs no host code |
  |<#DDD6FE> | **P11** Capability reference resolved against a registry |
  |<#FCA5A5> | **P7** Requires a Rust toolchain, or fails closed |
  |<#BFDBFE> | **P8** Existing runtime implementation, reached unchanged |
  |<#A7F3D0> | **P9** The fail-closed property this buys |
  |<#F1F5F9> | **P14** Out-of-band note (design rationale) |
endlegend
@enduml
